er 2024 as the parallel-run endpoint. Compulsory routing begins inclusively on 30 November 2024. The launch on 29 July and earlier circular dated 8 July are background dates. The packet does not specify a timestamp rule for attempted, received or resubmitted filings.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u4","u7","u9"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The earlier launch circular and existing IPD requests may clarify submission categories and operational treatment, but their contents are absent. The declared dependency external-authorities.24ec50 supplies no additional text. Nothing supplied makes the fixed transition date conditional on enhancement completion.","source_unit_ids":["u3","u7","u9"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["Does footnote 1 exhaustively delimit covered investment products, or describe the products currently administered by IPD?","What does the referenced 8 July 2024 circular say about supplementary submissions, pending applications and resubmissions after the transition?","Which event determines the submission date where transmission, receipt or acceptance occurs across the transition?","Do the existing IPD requests or referenced materials specify any operational exceptions or allocate responsibility among issuers, managers and submitting agents?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["The selected control is assessed for one actual application or submission event, not for an institution's overall compliance.","Extending the parallel-run period continues the existing-channel acceptance described in u4 through 29 November 2024.","The relevant submission date and classification are supplied as facts; disputed classifications and dates remain unknown.","No post-transition exception is inferred from enhancement plans, optional fee settlement or the enquiry provision."],"citations":[{"quote":"After the extended period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by the Investment Products Division (IPD)1 must be submitted to IPD via e-IP from 30 November 2024.","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"During this period, the SFC continues to accept applications and submissions via existing channels.","unit_id":"u4"},{"quote":"To facilitate these enhancements, the SFC will extend the parallel run period of e-IP by one month to 29 November 2024.","unit_id":"u7"},{"quote":"Starting 30 November 2024, ie, after the parallel run period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by IPD must be submitted via e-IP.","unit_id":"u9"},{"quote":"The current submission requests from IPD via the IP E-submission system will be integrated into e-IP, including reporting of net asset values, large redemptions and suspensions of dealing.","unit_id":"u9"},{"quote":"In addition, e-IP users can also settle recurring annual fees associated with relevant investment products through the new system.","unit_id":"u9"},{"quote":"The SFC will continue to review and enhance the operation of e-IP where practicable.","unit_id":"u11"},{"quote":"1 Investment-linked assurance schemes, mandatory provident fund products, open-ended fund companies, paper gold schemes, pooled retirement funds, real estate investment trusts, unit trusts and mutual funds and unlisted structured investment products.","unit_id":"u17"},{"quote":"Following the “Circular on launch of e-IP application/submission system on WINGS” dated 8 July 2024","unit_id":"u3"}],"distinction":"This reading applies the transition to submission events on or after the stated date, including relevant reporting submissions, without an express exemption for previously opened cases. It separates mandatory routing from optional fee payment and planned enhancements. The text does not sufficiently support a competing grandfathering or enhancement-dependent deadline rule; the strongest uncertainty is the classification and treatment of submissions within pending cases under the missing referenced materials.","family":"time","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The assessed event is an application or submission to IPD concerning an investment product administered by IPD, including a relevant reporting submission. A standalone fee payment is not classified as such solely because e-IP supports it. Product and event classification must be established from the applicable materials.","name":"is_covered_submission","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u9","u17"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Gregorian date attributed to the assessed submission event. If the controlling transmission, receipt or acceptance rule is unresolved, this fact remains unknown.","name":"submission_date","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u9"],"type":"date","unit":"Gregorian calendar date"},{"meaning":"The assessed application or submission was submitted to IPD through e-IP.","name":"submitted_via_eip","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u9"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"submitted_via_eip","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_covered_submission (>= submission_date (date 2024-11-30)))"},"local_id":"r1","questions":["Does supplementary material in a case opened before 30 November constitute a submission subject to the new route?","Are all categories listed in footnote 1 covered solely by category membership, or must IPD administration be separately established?","What operational evidence establishes submission through e-IP if transmission or acceptance fails?"],"statement":"Selected control—compulsory e-IP submission route: for an application or submission concerning an investment product administered by IPD, submission events dated 30 November 2024 or later must use e-IP. Existing channels remain available during the extended parallel run through 29 November. Relevant reporting requests are to be integrated into e-IP; the circular does not independently establish their reporting triggers. Annual-fee settlement through e-IP is optional. The stated transition is not expressly conditional on completion of enhancements.","subject":"Routing of an individual IPD investment-product application or submission at the November 2024 transition"}]},"controlled-language":{"coverage":[{"reason":"States the compulsory route and revised transition date.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u1"},{"reason":"Background heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u2"},{"reason":"Identifies e-IP, WINGS, launch history and an earlier circular whose contents are not supplied.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u3"},{"reason":"Establishes acceptance of existing channels during the original parallel run; read with the extension.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u4"},{"reason":"Heading connecting the extension and enhancements.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u5"},{"reason":"Describes monitoring and feedback, without imposing a submission duty.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u6"},{"reason":"Extends the parallel run through 29 November 2024 and explains its purpose.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u7"},{"reason":"Full-adoption heading supports the transition context.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u8"},{"reason":"Restates the mandatory route, identifies integrated reporting and distinguishes optional fee settlement.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u9"},{"reason":"Enquiries heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u10"},{"reason":"Review commitment and contact guidance; practicability qualifies enhancement, not the compulsory route.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u11"},{"reason":"Identifies the issuing division.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u12"},{"reason":"Identifies the issuing regulator.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u13"},{"reason":"End marker.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u14"},{"reason":"Product enumeration supports competing closed-list and descriptive-list scope readings.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u17"},{"reason":"Expands WINGS; does not establish an additional submission route.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u18"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension"